* Provenance: written for circsim from manufacturer datasheet parameters, MIT.
* These are in-house .model cards derived from published datasheet electrical
* characteristics (Vf @ If, Cj, trr, Vbr, Ir). No vendor model text is copied;
* only the numeric datasheet parameters (which are facts, not copyrightable
* expression) inform the standard ngspice level-1 diode parameter set.
*
* Diode parameter glossary (ngspice D model):
*   is  - saturation current      n   - emission coefficient
*   rs  - series resistance        cjo - zero-bias junction cap
*   tt  - transit time             bv  - reverse breakdown voltage
*   ibv - current at bv            vj  - junction potential
*   m   - grading coefficient      eg  - bandgap (eV)
*
* Forward drop is tuned via (is, n, rs) so that the simulated Vf at the
* datasheet test current matches the datasheet typical.

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 1N4148 / 1N914 small-signal fast switching silicon diode.
* Datasheet typ: Vf=0.72V @ 5mA, ~1.0V @ 100mA; trr=4ns; Cj=4pF; Vbr=100V.
.model D1N4148 D(is=2.52n rs=0.568 n=1.752 tt=20n cjo=4p vj=0.75 m=0.333
+ bv=100 ibv=100n eg=1.11)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 1N4001 general-purpose silicon rectifier (1A, 50V).
* Datasheet typ: Vf=0.93V @ 1A; trr slow (~3us-class); Cj~15pF; Vbr=50V.
.model D1N4001 D(is=14.1n rs=0.0337 n=1.984 tt=5u cjo=25.9p vj=0.325 m=0.44
+ bv=50 ibv=10u eg=1.11)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 1N5819 Schottky barrier rectifier (1A, 40V).
* Datasheet typ: Vf=0.6V @ 1A (low drop); Vbr=40V; higher Ir; eg lowered for
* the Schottky metal-semiconductor junction (~0.69 eV), n near 1.
.model D1N5819 D(is=31.7u rs=0.051 n=1.373 tt=4.32n cjo=140p vj=0.4 m=0.38
+ bv=40 ibv=1m eg=0.69 xti=2)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* SS54 / SB540 Schottky barrier rectifier (5A, 40V, DO-214AB/SMC).
* Datasheet typ: Vf=0.55V @ 5A (is/n set the junction drop, rs=30 mohm adds
* the ohmic part); Vbr=40V; Schottky eg=0.69 and xti=2, n near 1.
.model DSS54 D(is=2u rs=0.03 n=1.1 tt=8n cjo=300p vj=0.4 m=0.38
+ bv=40 ibv=1m eg=0.69 xti=2)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* SMAJ24A unidirectional 24V TVS (SMA, 400W): standoff 24V, breakdown
* 26.7-29.5V @ 1mA (bv/ibv), clamping 38.9V @ 10.3A. The exponential breakdown
* only adds ~n*Vt*ln(Ipp/ibv) ~ 0.24V from 1mA to 10.3A, so rs=1.16 supplies
* the remaining (38.9-26.7-0.24)/10.3 ~ 1.16 ohm of clamp slope. Forward path
* is an ordinary Si diode; Cj~280pF.
.model DSMAJ24A D(is=1e-12 rs=1.16 n=1 cjo=280p vj=0.75 m=0.333
+ bv=26.7 ibv=1m eg=1.11)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* BZX55C5V1 / 5V1 zener diode (Vz=5.1V @ 5mA).
* Reverse breakdown modeled via bv/ibv; forward path is an ordinary Si diode.
.model DZ5V1 D(is=1n rs=0.5 n=1.7 tt=50n cjo=175p vj=0.75 m=0.333
+ bv=5.1 ibv=5m eg=1.11)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* BZX84C3V0 / 3V0 zener diode (Vz=3.0V @ 1mA - soft low-voltage knee).
* Reverse breakdown modeled via bv/ibv; forward path is an ordinary Si diode.
.model DZ3V0 D(is=1n rs=0.6 n=1.7 tt=50n cjo=450p vj=0.75 m=0.333
+ bv=3.0 ibv=1m eg=1.11)
